| !Run for !Matinee (a Plex, Jellyfin and DLNA client with a built-in player)
| Puts Matinee on the icon bar: Select on it to add a server, or to browse
| the one in use. Videos play in Matinee's own window (riscos-ffmpeg's player
| core), or in ReelEGL or Reel if chosen on the Player menu.
Set Matinee$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <Matinee$Dir>.!Sprites

RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error Matinee needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error Matinee needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
| Threads: the thread timer of UnixLib 5.0.1 and later (Matinee is built with 5.0.3.3)
| runs from the PThreadTicker module when it's loaded: a copy merged into
| !System first, else the one in here. Without it UnixLib uses a copy in
| the RMA, which also works.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere System:Modules.PThrTicker Then RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere <Matinee$Dir>.PThrTicker Then RMLoad <Matinee$Dir>.PThrTicker
| https (plex.tv, and servers' plex.direct addresses): RISC OS's AcornSSL
| module (RISC OS 5.28 or later); quiet if it's missing (then signing in
| with a code says so, and only a server's own http address works)
RMEnsure AcornSSL 0 IfThere System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL Then RMLoad System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL
| The picture scaled by the display: the VideoOverlay module (in !System on
| RISC OS 5); quiet if it's missing (then the picture is plotted instead)
RMEnsure VideoOverlay 0.00 IfThere System:Modules.VideoOverlay Then RMLoad System:Modules.VideoOverlay
| Sound: SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager (ssb.zip, from
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html) and SharedSound
| (part of RISC OS). Merged into !System they still have to be loaded:
| these do it (and are quiet if they're missing).
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer

| The program is about 32MB (the player, and FFmpeg's format and codec
| lists); the posters, pictures and sound are in a dynamic area ("Matinee Heap").
| The player's log (<Wimp$ScrapDir>.MatineeLog) is off unless asked for:
| *Set Matinee$Log on (or a file's name) before starting Matinee
If "<Matinee$Log>" = "" Then Set Matinee$Log off
WimpSlot -min 40960K -max 40960K
Run <Matinee$Dir>.!RunImage %*0
